{"files": [{"id": 42161545, "name": "pgen.1010903.g006.tif", "size": 3141204, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/42161545", "supplied_md5": "6b8bb9dc006a8c9fe3a7634b2f99b04b", "computed_md5": "6b8bb9dc006a8c9fe3a7634b2f99b04b", "mimetype": "image/tiff"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 842833, "full_name": "Karine Normandin", "first_name": "Karine", "last_name": "Normandin", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 126532, "full_name": "Jasmin Coulombe-Huntington", "first_name": "Jasmin", "last_name": "Coulombe-Huntington", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 16892359, "full_name": "Corinne St-Denis", "first_name": "Corinne", "last_name": "St-Denis", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 16892362, "full_name": "Alexandre Bernard", "first_name": "Alexandre", "last_name": "Bernard", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 9592382, "full_name": "Mohammed Bourouh", "first_name": "Mohammed", "last_name": "Bourouh", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 470436, "full_name": "Thierry Bertomeu", "first_name": "Thierry", "last_name": "Bertomeu", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1118, "full_name": "Mike Tyers", "first_name": "Mike", "last_name": "Tyers", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Mike_Tyers", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 73964, "full_name": "Vincent Archambault", "first_name": "Vincent", "last_name": "Archambault", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Vincent_Archambault", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/Inactivation_of_KIF18A_enhances_nuclear_reassembly_defects_after_mitosis_in_PLK1-compromised_cells_/24044785", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p><b>A.</b> Time-lapse images of RPE-1 cells expressing H2B-GFP and \u03b1-Tub-mRFP and treated as indicated. BI2536 was added at the IC<sub>30</sub> concentration (5 nM). The top cell treated with BI2536 and a non-target siRNA reassembled the nucleus normally. The bottom cell treated with BI2536 and siRNA against KIF18A assembled micronuclei (arrowheads) after mitosis. The time prior to anaphase onset was set as time zero. <b>B.</b> RPE-1 cells expressing H2B-GFP and \u03b1-Tub-mRFP and treated as indicated were fixed and stained for Lamin A (white) and DAPI (blue). Note the structural nuclear defects occurring when KIF18A or SKA1 is depleted in the presence of BI2536 at the IC<sub>30</sub>. <b>C-D.</b> Quantification of solidity (C) and circularity (D) of the nucleus in cells treated as indicated. Averages \u00b1SD are shown. *** p < 0.001, ** p < 0.01, * p < 0.05 in Student\u2019s unpaired T test. ns: non-significant. Coordinate values used to generate graphs are available in <a href=\"http://www.plosgenetics.org/article/info:doi/10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903#pgen.1010903.s022\" target=\"_blank\">S6 Data</a>.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 3141204, "created_date": "2023-08-28T17:34:05Z", "modified_date": "2023-09-08T18:01:50Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["xlink \"> polo", "wide screening strategy", "threonine kinase required", "spindle assembly checkpoint", "like kinase 1", "cell division cycle", "compromised cells resulted", "nuclear reassembly defects", "different kinetochore perturbations", "rendering cells hypersensitive", "partial plk1 inactivation", "partial plk1 inhibition", "partial inhibition", "cancer cells", "often hypersensitive", "mitotic defects", "kinetochore complex", "plk1 compromises", "plk1 activity", "results suggest", "promising target", "notably factors", "multiple ways", "genetic enhancers", "functionally linked", "extremely sensitive", "dependent 